ing by Belgian painter Alfred Stevens. This painting is representative of the early part of Stevens' career, when he was keen on representing the squalor of the time through realist painting.","What is Called Vagrancy"],"17492697":["The Bath is an oil on canvas painting by Belgian painter Alfred Stevens. Apparently, two version of the paintings existed, one of which was reportedly destroyed in one of Vienna's fires.","The Bath (Stevens)"],"18225338":["Mary Magdalene is an oil on canvas painting by Belgian painter Alfred Stevens. It is Stevens' revision of the Biblical figure of Mary Magdalene.","Mary Magdalene (Stevens)"],"18225426":["La parisienne japonaise is an oil on canvas painting by Belgian painter Alfred Stevens. It depicts a young woman in a blue kimono standing in front of a mirror.","La parisienne japonaise"],"19973926":["The Psyché is an oil on panel painting by the Belgian artist Alfred Stevens. Painted in circa 1871, the painting once belonged to Robert de Montesquiou, and is currently housed at the Princeton University Art Museum located in Princeton, New Jersey.","The Psyché (My Studio)"],"21618973":["The Parisian Sphinx is an oil-on-canvas painting by Belgian painter Alfred Stevens. Painted between 1875 and 1877, it depicts a dreamy young woman gently supporting her head with her hand.","The Parisian Sphinx"],"47498727":["Camille Lemonnier in the Artist's Studio is an oil on canvas painting by Belgian painter Alfred Stevens. The portrait was for many years part of a private collection in Paris, but in 2015 it was purchased by the Heritage Found, and is currently housed at the Royal Museums of Fine Arts in Brussels.","Camille Lemonnier in the Artist's Studio"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}